+# Provisioning Runbook — Representative Hardware (HIL / RT / Accelerator Nodes)
+
+Purpose
+-------
+Step-by-step operator runbook to procure, network, join, label and validate representative hardware and give CI access.
+
+Preconditions
+- Kube admin credentials (kubeconfig) or cluster admin access.
+- SSH/BMC access or bastion host for lab network.
+- CI credentials (GITHUB_TOKEN) to create issues/secrets.
+
+Steps
+1. Procurement & rack setup
+   - Order devices: at least 1 GPU node (NVIDIA A100/RTX), 1 RT robot / RT node, 1 HIL rack with adapters.
+   - Ensure management network & power redundancy; assign management IPs.
+
+2. Network & access
+   - Verify SSH or BMC connectivity from bastion/CI runner.
+   - Ensure URLs reachable from CI runners; create firewall rules if necessary.
+
+3. Join cluster
+   - Install kubelet and kubeadm (or use provider) and join the target cluster.
+   - Confirm node appears in `kubectl get nodes`.
+
+4. Label nodes
+   - Apply labels:
+     - `kubectl label node <name> aegis/gpu=true`
+     - `kubectl label node <name> aegis/rt=true`
+     - `kubectl label node <name> aegis/hil=true`
+
+5. Driver & firmware pinning
+   - Run driver installer/pinning steps per ops/installers/driver_installer_manager.py.
+   - Bake or validate golden image per ops/images/bake_golden_image.sh.
+   - Ensure driver_versions.json aligns and commit to repo if changes needed.
+
+6. Run validation
+   - Apply DaemonSet: `kubectl apply -f ops/ci/driver_daemonset_job.yaml`
+   - Collect per-node diagnostics from `/tmp/driver_installer_diag.json`.
+   - Run `python ops/provisioning/label_and_validate_nodes.py --nodes <node1,node2> --label aegis/gpu=true`
+
+7. Add CI secrets
+   - Add node credentials / HIL adapter tokens to CI secret store.
+   - Add ACME_HIL_URL / ACME_HIL_TOKEN for HIL runner integration.
+
+8. Smoke HIL run
+   - Run a short campaign: `python ops/hil/run_hil_campaign.py --manifest ops/hil/playbook/example_replay_manifest.json --repeats 3`
+   - Ensure determinism and WCET evidence is produced in evidence store.
+
+Acceptance criteria
+- Each requested device family has >=1 labeled CI-reachable node.
+- Driver validation DaemonSet reports success across nodes.
+- Short HIL run completes with evidence indexed in Postgres.
+
+Rollback & remediation
+- If driver validation fails, collect logs and open issue with vendor & infra teams.
+- If node cannot join cluster, check network/BMC and re-run join procedure.
+
