+# Attestation Runbook — TPM Integration & OTA gating
+
+Purpose
+-------
+Detailed steps to perform production TPM attestation integration, AK management and OTA gating.
+
+Steps
+1. Provision verifier host
+   - Harden a verifier host (private network), install `tpm2-tools` and `openssl`.
+   - Ensure restricted access (VPN/SVC account) and logging/audit enabled.
+
+2. Generate / provision AKs
+   - On each device, provision an Attestation Key (AK) and record the public part (AK_PUB).
+   - Store AK_PUBs in a secure store (Vault or verifier host).
+
+3. Configure verifier
+   - Place AK pub keys at /opt/ak_pub.pem (or a mapping).
+   - Deploy ops/attestation/production_tpm_verifier.py behind authenticated API.
+
+4. OTA integration
+   - Deploy integrations/ota/ota_with_attestation_service.py in staging.
+   - Set AK_PUB_PATH env and OTA_BUCKET.
+   - Ensure OTA endpoint only returns presigned URLs when verifier returns ok.
+
+5. E2E tests
+   - Use `ops/robot/attestation/generate_mtls_certs.sh` to generate test certs.
+   - Use tpm_quote_client or hardware to produce real quotes and verify end-to-end with `Attestation E2E Test` workflow.
+
+6. Security audit
+   - Schedule third-party audit covering AK management, verifier host, CA policy, OTA endpoints and KMS/Vault usage.
+
+Acceptance
+- OTA refuses activation if verifier denial.
+- Verifier logs are stored and auditable for at least 90 days.
+- Third-party audit completed and high-risk findings remediated.
