+# Managed Services Migration Runbook
+
+Purpose
+-------
+Step-by-step migration from in-cluster Postgres/Redis to managed RDS/Cloud SQL + Managed Redis/Kafka + pgbouncer.
+
+Procedure
+1. Provision managed resources
+   - Create managed Postgres (multi-AZ), retrieve connection string.
+   - Create managed Redis/Kafka; retrieve endpoint(s).
+   - Provision pgbouncer (helm chart or managed).
+
+2. Network & secrets
+   - Ensure private connectivity (VPC peering).
+   - Insert secrets into Vault / CI secret store (DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL).
+
+3. Initialize schema
+   - Run: `DATABASE_URL=<managed> python ops/db/postgres_connector.py --init`
+
+4. Data migration (maintenance window)
+   - `pg_dump` local and `pg_restore` into managed DB using secure channel.
+   - Validate row counts and indexes.
+
+5. Smoke tests
+   - Run: `python ops/db/migration/run_migration_smoke.py`
+   - Run worker_postgres in staging and process sample tasks.
+
+6. Cut-over (canary)
+   - Update configmap for one service to managed DATABASE_URL and deploy.
+   - Monitor for 24-72h; if stable, roll more services.
+
+7. Rollback plan
+   - Keep local DB snapshot and credential to quickly switch config map back to original database.
+
+Acceptance
+- Smoke tests pass and worker_postgres successfully indexes evidence into managed Postgres.
+- Redis/Kafka latency acceptable and tested under load.
+
